<title>MACAU: Macau airport signs apron extension contract.</title>
<headline>Macau airport signs apron extension contract.</headline>
<text>
<p>MACAU, OCT 25 (REUTER) - The Macau International Airport Co signed a 50 million pataca (US$6.25 million) contract with the Portuguese building firm Sociedade de Construcoes Soares da Costa S.A. for an extension of the airport south apron, a spokesman said on Friday.</p>
<p>The spokesman for the airport company, Concessionaria do Aeroporto de Macau (CAM), said the contract was signed Thursday in Macau.</p>
<p>The extension, expected to be completed by mid-1997, will be the first since the airport was officially opened last December. It would incorporate about 47,000 square metres of additional apron.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843-6345</p>
</text>
